!!! 'then' is optional in value position.
!!!
!!! The statement form reads "when c then ...", so an author transfers that
!!! shape to the value form and writes "when c then give a". That was
!!! rejected, and the asymmetry had no meaning behind it: 'give' is what
!!! marks the value, and it is still required. Both spellings are accepted
!!! here, in a plain conditional and in every kind of 'consider' arm.
book tour.value-position-then

state begin choice
    when Idle
    when Busy holding number
end choice

main returns number begin paragraph
    value n as number is 2

    !!! Value position WITH 'then' -- the shape the statement form teaches.
    value a as text is when n is greater than 1 then give "many" otherwise give "one" end when

    !!! Value position WITHOUT 'then' -- still accepted, unchanged.
    value b as text is when n is greater than 1 give "many" otherwise give "one" end when

    value c as text is consider n
        when 1 then give "one"
        when 2 give "two"
        otherwise give "other"
    end consider

    value here as state is state.Busy holding 7
    value d as text is consider here
        when state.Busy holding amount then give "busy"
        when state.Idle give "idle"
        otherwise give "unknown"
    end consider

    say a
    say b
    say c
    say d
    give 0
end paragraph
